<div class="legal-page">
  <h1 class="page-title">From the founder</h1>
  <p class="updated-date">Kent Mayer, founder of PreCheckd</p>

  <div class="content-card">
    <h2>Why I built PreCheckd</h2>
    <p>I have spent more than 20 years working in insurance, cybersecurity, IT and project management. Different industries, same lesson: almost every good outcome starts with trust, and trust is expensive to check.</p>
    <p>Hiring is where that shows up the most. A candidate has to trust that the recruiter is real and the job is real. A recruiter has to trust that the person on the resume can do what the resume says. Today both sides mostly guess.</p>

    <h2>What I want to fix</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Fake and unverified recruiters.</strong> Candidates should know who is really contacting them before they share anything. Every recruiter on PreCheckd is verified first.</li>
      <li><strong>Resumes that can't be checked.</strong> Candidates can prove what they know with skill tests, and recruiters see a clear level instead of a claim.</li>
      <li><strong>A process that wastes everyone's time.</strong> Verified people on both sides means fewer dead ends, less guessing and faster conversations.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How I'm building it</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Candidates stay in control. You choose which results recruiters can see.</li>
      <li>Levels, not grades, so a result is hard to misread.</li>
      <li>Messages are scanned for spam, scams and malware, and anyone can report a scam.</li>
      <li>Small, honest tools that do one job well, rather than a pile of features.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Where it goes from here</h2>
    <p>PreCheckd is new, and the first people who join will shape it. If something is confusing, broken or missing, I want to hear about it. Write to me at <a href="mailto:kent@precheckd.com">kent@precheckd.com</a>.</p>

    <p>Thank you for being early.</p>
    <p><strong>Kent Mayer</strong><br>Founder, PreCheckd</p>
  </div>
</div>
